sequenceDiagram
    participant A as billing:run (A)
    participant B as billing:run (B, same moment)
    participant DB as MySQL

    A->>DB: read clock, servers and ip assignments
    B->>DB: read clock, servers and ip assignments
    Note over A,B: each works out ALL hours due up to now<br/>(a long pause just means more hours)
    A->>DB: BEGIN, INSERT charge (server 7, 10:00)
    B->>DB: BEGIN, INSERT charge (server 7, 10:00)
    Note over B,DB: B waits on the unique key<br/>(billable_type, billable_id, hour_start)
    A->>DB: INSERT ledger entry (key charge:server:7:...T10)
    A->>DB: COMMIT
    DB-->>B: duplicate key
    Note over B: skipped, nothing written
    Note over A: if A dies before COMMIT, MySQL rolls back:<br/>no charge without its money movement, B or the next run does it
